# CKKS precision propagation: accuracy and estimator time

Maintainer summary; the solver-facing statement is
agent-base/frontier/task/repo/README.md.

Submit a tar containing payload/solution.patch against the provided repository.
Files below estimator/ are editable except the fixed set (experiment programs,
stats.go, utils.go, go.mod, go.sum, and the DFTMatrix type with GenMatrices in
dft.go). Maximum patch size is 262144 bytes and maximum changed files is 32.

Every configuration is measured as three interleaved pairs of complete
invocations, candidate and reference, with fresh keys and randomness. A pass
requires both accuracy statistics within their frozen band of the reference on
every configuration and a strictly lower trusted estimator clock in every pair
of every configuration. The continuous score depends on accuracy only.

Development feedback measures the six base development configurations with one
pair each and gates nothing; final measures 29 with three pairs. Answering
window 18000 s, train pool 7200 s / 100 calls, independent final 600 s. Each role has 2 CPUs;
Agent memory 2048 MiB, Verifier 4096 MiB, workspace 8192 MiB.

This release has no frozen accuracy bands. Evaluations report
calibration_pending and cannot pass until the reference calibration has been
collected on this source and a metadata successor carries the frozen bands.
